# ==========================================
# macOS AppleDouble metadata — v0.83.1
# ==========================================
# ⚠️ Over a thousand of these were sitting in the tree, uncommitted-but-
# untracked and INVISIBLE IN FINDER. macOS writes a `._foo.tsx` sidecar
# next to `foo.tsx` when a file with extended attributes is copied to a
# non-HFS volume — which is what every `ordence-v*` zip and tarball
# round-trip did.
#
# They matter because they are hidden on a Mac and ORDINARY FILES ON
# LINUX. Pushed to GitHub, Railway checks out `app/platform/._page.tsx` —
# a binary blob wearing a .tsx extension — alongside the real one.
#
# TypeScript and Next both happen to skip dotfiles, so this was noise
# rather than a build break. "Happens to" is not a guarantee worth
# depending on across a toolchain upgrade.
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Local backup zips produced by scripts/ — never commit a 5 MB artefact.
ordence-full-backup-*.zip

# debug logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

